  "id": "MAL-2026-20326",
  "summary": "Malicious code in @c1-ease/bank (npm)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (15ba6783ba51366782fa289b444f655cd026cc5ac82d3fae5a5e9f256961c954)\nThe package declares a `postinstall` script that runs `node beacon.cjs`, and `index.js` re-invokes the same beacon on require. The beacon collects `os.hostname()`, `__dirname`, `process.cwd()`, the Node version, and the package name and POSTs them as JSON to the hardcoded endpoint `https://vmi3699893.contaboserver.net:8787/_ah/dc`, a bare Contabo VPS unrelated to any declared publisher. TLS certificate verification is explicitly disabled via `rejectUnauthorized: false`. Beyond the beacon, `index.js` exports a Proxy whose every property returns a no-op function; the package advertises itself as a `Compatibility shim` under the `@c1-ease` scope but ships no real functionality, consistent with a dependency-confusion or install-tracking artifact targeting a potentially confusable scope name. Installing or requiring the package causes host identifiers to be sent to an attacker-controlled destination with TLS verification disabled.\n",
